  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let current through galvanometer be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and current through shunt resistance be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/24402c0e-0a4c-4918-a8c9-9eb06f0bc99f-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 120px;\" /></p><p>Given figure of merit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Then, total current,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mfenced><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>S</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>K</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mi>S</mi></mfrac></math></p>",
